SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ssttttyy utility is compliant with the IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”)
     specification.

     The flags [--eeff], the operands aallttwweerraassee, ccoollss, ccoolluummnnss, ccrrtt, ccrrttssccttss,
     ddeecc, eecchhookkee, eexxttpprroocc, fflluusshhoo, iimmaaxxbbeell, kkeerrnniinnffoo, mmddmmbbuuff, oonnllccrr, oonnooeeoott,
     oossttaarrtt, oossttoopp, ooxxttaabbss, ppeennddiinn, rroowwss, ssiizzee, ssppeeeedd, and ttttyy, and the con‐
     trol characters eol2, dsusp, lnext, reprint, status, and werase are all
     extensions to that specification.

     The operands iiuuccllcc, oollccuucc, and xxccaassee are marked by IEEE Std 1003.1-2008
     (“POSIX.1”) as legacy items; the operands listed in _C_o_m_p_a_t_i_b_i_l_i_t_y _m_o_d_e_s
     can also be considered legacy.

     The operands bbss00--11, ccrr00--33, ffff00--11, nnll00--11, ooccrrnnll, ooffddeell, ooffiillll, oonnllrreett,
     oonnooccrr, rraaww, ttaabb00--33, ttaabbss, and vvtt00--11 are marked by IEEE Std 1003.1-2008
     (“POSIX.1”) as being an X/Open System Interfaces option.  Of those, only
     ooccrrnnll, oonnllrreett, oonnooccrr, rraaww, and ttaabbss are supported by this implementation
     of ssttttyy, and behaviour for ttaabbss differs.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A ssttttyy command appeared in Version 2 AT&T UNIX.

